WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
A small radioactive
source sits in its holder,

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.870
handled with tongs.

3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.260
You can't see what comes out of it.

4
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.630
A detector beside it
just clicks, at random.

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.010
And it clicks even when
no source is there at all.

6
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.800
So with just a sheet of paper
and a thin strip of metal,

7
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.520
how could you tell what the source emits?

8
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.390
In this mission, you'll
set up a fair test:

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.780
fix the source and the detector,
and change only the absorber.

10
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:32.180
Then you'll find out how many counts you
need before a reading can be trusted.

11
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.230
Your mission: explain how a sheet of paper
and a thin strip of metal reveal what

12
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.430
a source emits.
